crosoft/vcpkg/issues/537#issuecomment-273705690","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/537","id":273705690,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3MzcwNTY5MA==","user":{"login":"marcojez","id":15309612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzA5NjEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15309612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez","html_url":"https://github.com/marcojez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcojez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-01-19T07:57:47Z","updated_at":"2017-01-19T07:57:47Z","body":"I figured out what's happening. Those executables are only built if GLFW is found by CMake (see source/tools/*/CMakeLists.txt). GLFW is not listed as a dependency for glbinding, so it will only break on systems where package glfw3 is present (that's my case).\r\n\r\nglbinding's cmake files don't offer the choice to exclude those tools from the build process, so deleting the executables at the end (if they were generated) is probably the only way to solve this issue.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/comments/273705690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"marcojez","id":15309612,"node